oment but  i guess i was just kind of shocked and  in a good way i mean by  how long that lasted and also the fact  that they did that with your two  characters  in particular i know i mean it's brutal  like my mom my mom stopped watching at  that point she couldn't take it  could not take it and i couldn't either  i was just like oh my god it's kind of  it's very disturbing to watch this but  um  yeah in the moment i really had no idea  what was happening um  because you know obviously like my eyes  were closed and like there was you know  blood everywhere so seeing it  how it actually looked was was pretty  cool i'd never worked with um  mouth blood before so that was that was  an exciting first for me  sometimes we play a movie and tv themed  would you rather and that makes me think  of one of the questions we often ask and  it's  would you rather have to fake sneeze or  fake vomit in a scene and let's throw in  would you  rather have to fake sneeze fake vomit or  fake cough up blood in a scene  i mean honestly the coffin of blood it  wasn't as hard as i thought it was gonna  be  it was actually kind of fun um  yeah so i guess i would have to do the  the coughing up blood because i think  i've i think i've got that down at this  point  can confirm uh did you get the chance to  cross over at all with gillian while you  were shooting so you could discuss the  character transition at all  no i still have never met her to this  day  so youtube are so convincing too oh good  i'm so glad yeah i hadn't even seen any  videos of her performance so i was  really nervous  it was you know just hoping that our  interpretations of the character on  paper  were able to translate on screen in the  same way and kind of carry over into the  films and  and and seem like the same person i was  really glad that that it did  and a lot of the characteristics were  the same but yeah never met her never  discussed the character but  hopefully i get to meet her soon yes  very very very impressive job well done  in that department so  thank you with this one i know there was  a lot of stranger things crossover in  terms of the folks behind the camera and  also in front of it so when you jump  onto a set like this does it kind of  feel like  an extension of that home or still a  completely different project  it's a different story i mean yeah there  was a lot of we filmed in atlanta  so a lot of the crew was um the same  and so that was really nice it was kind  of comforting to see these people that i  was familiar with  and also lee our director uh is married  to ross one of the duffer brothers so i  had known lee since i was like 14 years  old  so it was really exciting to get to work  with her because it was something that i  had been wanting to do  when did you uh first start talking  about doing this project together  the script just kind of got sent to me  like the audition got sent to me and i  was like  oh i mean it's lee like i have to do  this i have to go after this and then  i met with her we've read through some  scenes talked about the project  and then um we did a chemistry read with  um emily who plays cindy and yeah and  then after that  we're like okay let's do this and i'm  just happy that it worked out  also in the stranger things sphere i do  definitely see some similar qualities  that ziggy  and max share just in terms of who they  are as people and  i also have the loss of a sibling on my  mind so having filmed  this before going back to that do you  find that any qualities of  ziggy's are coming through when you're  playing max now  it's hard to say um just because  depending on what season i feel like the  characters  we have a lot of time at being a series  the characters really grow and develop  and each season they're almost like a  different person  um so i guess there are a few  similarities  they're definitely two strong female  characters but  um one thing that did that i did  take with me from from fear street is  just like my experience with stunts now  i think i feel like  i've i've got a lot more experience and  that's  helped me along the way i like that  tease quite a bit  also i wanted to ask you something about  the stranger things season four  production schedule because i know it  was a very unique experience on that one  so  what would you say is one unique pro of  filming  season four something that's you know  better than ever and then  what's something that proved to be more  challenging that you had to adjust to in  order to overcome  i mean yeah so we started filming season  four  i don't even know when it was but it was  before the pandemic and then we had  we got like a month of filming done then  we had to stop  for i guess seven or eight months and  then we came back to work and things  were like completely different so i  think  the real challenging part was just  adjusting to the to the new  the new rules and the regulations that  were in place on set that was a big  adjustment  but yeah and i think we were just all  just so grateful to be able to work  and yeah we've been working working for  a while now and  and creating something really amazing  the scale of the show just gets bigger  and bigger each year  um so yeah it's just been really  incredible  to see where they're going with the  storyline which it's really amazing this  year and just how the stakes are just  so much higher higher than they've ever  been i don't envy you having to tease  that all the time but you got a lot of  people out there so excited and  all i want to do right now is tell  everybody out there how good you are in  fear street and how good fear street is  overall  i freaking loved it and cannot convey  that strongly enough  oh thank you so much

